    "result_text": "The sheet's due-total and overdue-total now leave out the single highest and single lowest person's figure once three or more people have one. All 4 tests in `bin/e2e` pass.\n\n**Server (`Rollup.java`):** The sheet totals are worked out in one place, and that feeds the TOTALS audit line. It now keeps a list of each person's figures and adds them up through a new `trimmedSum`. A person whose due-total is n/a isn't in the due list. Every person is in the overdue list, since an overdue-total is always a figure. With fewer than three figures nothing is trimmed.\n\n**Front end (`features/claims/claims.ts`):** The totals row and the header get their totals from the same function, `useSheetTotals`. It now uses a matching `trimmedSum` helper. The overdue-total used to be one sum over all overdue claims. It is now worked out per person and then trimmed. The overdue *count* still covers every person: the request only asks to trim the totals, and the test expects it that way.\n\nPer-person figures, per-grade and per-period totals, backing and the claimed total are unchanged.",
